# Build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The application's own runtime data.
#
# Claims Manager keeps its database, document store and demo accounts file in
# the same folder as the executable. In a normal build that is bin\Debug or
# bin\Release, already covered above - but these patterns catch the case where
# somebody runs a copy from the repository root.
#
# demo-accounts.csv holds a password. It is a fictional one, shared across five
# invented accounts, but a credentials file in version control is a habit worth
# not forming, and secret scanners will flag it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Claims.mdb
Claims.ldb
Claims.laccdb
Documents/
demo-accounts.csv
write-probe-*.tmp

# Installer output. The MSI is a build artefact; publish releases instead.
Installer/*.msi
Installer/*.wixpdb
Installer/*.wixobj
Installer/*.cab

# A pre-seeded database for the optional PreSeededDatabase component is a local
# convenience, not something to version.
Installer/Claims.mdb

# Report exports, if anyone saves them into the tree
*.xlsx
*.xls

# Misc
*.orig
*.bak
*.log
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
